                                                              "summary":  "Brown argues that Wall Street\u0027s skepticism about AI infrastructure overbuilding fundamentally misreads the demand curveÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Âcurrent AI applications like chatbots and coding assistants are primitive compared to the autonomous agent and robotics workloads coming. He points to hyperscaler cloud revenue growth (Azure +43%, AWS +37%, Google Cloud +82%) as evidence of sustained demand, and notes that the trillions being committed represent multi-decade investment theses, not near-term bets. His core contention is that a world with a billion people running personal AI agents will require far more compute than exists today, making the capex buildout necessary rather than speculative.",
