                                                              "summary":  "Brown profiles Ron Baron\u0027s remarkable 40-year track record, during which Baron Capital grew from $10 million to roughly $70 billion in AUM by holding concentrated long-term positions in transformative companies. Key wins include Tesla (entered at a split-adjusted ~$14/share in 2014, now a $5B position) and SpaceX (now a $25B stake). Baron\u0027s current prediction is that SpaceX could reach a $20 trillion valuation, making it the world\u0027s largest company. Brown frames the lesson as the power of conviction-based, decade-long holdingÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Âignoring mainstream skepticism in favor of rigorous business analysis.",
