                                                                                "take":  "Santoli is calling a phase transition, not a cycle top, and that distinction matters enormously for portfolio construction. Phase-transition markets tend to redistribute returns from momentum holders to fundamental analysts -- the stocks that re-rate from here will be the ones with actual cash-flow proof points, not the ones with the best AI story. This is the moment when Damodaran\u0027s framework becomes most useful: discount-rate discipline applied to real earnings beats narrative-driven multiples. Investors who survived the hype phase by holding winners now face the harder task of deciding which of those holdings has durable earnings power versus which was riding a sentiment wave.",
